& [CanonicalIdentity] is bounded language-purpose authority
  + [canonical_uuid] is 5fb9bea9-248d-4051-a69b-778ab243096e
  + [profile] is sop-multi-target-semantic-compiler/0.1
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is a90af861-ccb4-433f-964d-eff53d7457ad
  + [requirement_set] is SMTC-001 through SMTC-030
  + [authority_grade] is semantic_language_purpose
  + [canonical_source_specification] is this file

& [PurposeIdentity] is multi-target semantic programming
  + SOP articulates intended meaning through identities, contexts, relations, conditions, contracts, instructions, programs, states, transitions, effects, judgments, faults, proofs, and residuals
  + explicit SemanticProgram regions may compile into multiple target forms while retaining one source identity and semantic center
  + plain articulated meaning remains inspectable before and after compilation
  + the language is self-describing in principle but retains an independently trusted bootstrap
  = must: distinguish language purpose from implementation maturity
  - never: claim that the current repository contains a complete compiler merely because its purpose is canonical

& [ArtifactRoleBoundary] preserves the existing SOP corpus
  + [source_document] is preserved input and non-executable
  + [definition] establishes semantic environment and is non-executable
  + [data] supplies inspectable values and is non-executable
  + [contract] constrains admitted programs and is non-executable
  + [program] is an executable candidate only after complete admission
  + [policy] governs gates and is non-executable
  + [profile] narrows language, target, or runtime behavior and is compiler metadata unless it contains explicit program regions
  + [test_or_fixture] is executable only in its declared isolated harness
  + [proof] records evidence and is non-executable
  + [narrative] records history and reentry and is non-executable
  + [package_manifest] binds lineage and is compiler or trust metadata
  + [mixed] is non-executable by default and requires exact per-region roles
  + unclassified historical SOP is preserved and non-executable
  = must: bind role to exact source generation and region
  - never: infer program role from syntax, filename, directory, imperative wording, graph proximity, or signature presence

& [ProgramAdmission] is the only normal execution route
  + role and region closure passes
  + source, profile, dependency, version, freshness, and provenance pass
  + names, contexts, namespaces, imports, kinds, types, relations, and authorities resolve
  + purpose, inputs, preconditions, assumptions, invariants, permissions, obligations, prohibitions, outputs, effects, faults, and termination are complete
  + state, transitions, control, effects, capabilities, budgets, and targets validate
  + lowering retains source maps, correspondence, diagnostics, loss, and proof obligations
  + conformance and negative fixtures required by the profile pass
  + trusted package identity, signatures, scope, validity, dependencies, and revocation pass
  + runtime entry, inputs, granted authority, capabilities, effects, and budget match
  = must: fail closed on unknown, ambiguous, conflicting, stale, unsupported, unauthorised, lossy, or incomplete conditions

& [StageSeparation] is typed
  + describe articulates possible meaning
  + declare modifies a SemanticEnvironment under declaration semantics
  + compile creates candidate IR and target artifacts
  + propose returns a candidate judgment, route, plan, artifact, or effect
  + evaluate applies pure or inference semantics
  + validate checks declared conditions
  + authorize grants bounded permission from eligible authority
  + commit applies an admitted state or external effect transition
  + observe records resulting state and may report unknown or partial outcome
  - never: let an earlier stage impersonate a later one

& [CanonicalSemanticCenter] is one source-mapped SemanticIR
  + every node has stable identity within the exact compilation
  + every node maps to source spans or explicit generated-node derivation
  + document and region roles remain attached
  + kinds, types, relations, contracts, state, effects, authority requests, faults, uncertainty, and proof obligations are explicit
  + serialization is deterministic under the same accepted source, profile, dependencies, and compiler generation
  + target-local representations remain subordinate projections
  - never: infer identity, subtype, truth, or authority from labels, embeddings, graph distance, or backend representation alone

& [CompilerSemanticContract] is role-first and target-neutral
  + parsing recognizes one explicit versioned LanguageProfile without deciding execution role
  + static passes run in order: role closure; source and dependency integrity; name, context, and import resolution; kind, type, and relation validation; contract completeness; state, transition, and control validation; authority, capability, and effect validation; target capability and loss validation; termination and budget validation; proof-obligation formation
  + module identity is UUID, immutable version, and digest
  + imports are exact, cycles are restricted, initialization is explicit, and authority does not transitively widen
  + standard-library behavior is ordinary versioned modules except for the minimum semantic constructors needed to express and check the language
  + optimizations require equivalence proof or declared approximation and preserve effects, authority, faults, provenance, and contracts
  + diagnostics bind stage, severity, code, spans, identities, expected, actual, repairs, causal chain, and authority consequence

& [CommonTargetABI] is the compiler-backend seam
  + request contains compiler identity, SemanticIR root, source map, contract set, module closure, target profile, capabilities, authority request, proof policy, and budget
  + response contains target artifacts, correspondence manifest, diagnostics, proofs, loss records, provider dependencies, nondeterminism record, and target manifest
  + support status is exact_supported, supported_with_declared_approximation, provider_dependent, or unsupported
  + unsupported required features, prohibited loss, missing proof, missing capability, or incompatible ABI version release no executable artifact
  + compilation never substitutes for trusted-package or runtime admission

& [RuntimeABI] is the admission-and-evaluation seam
  + request contains package identity, entry point, typed inputs, source and SemanticIR roots, target artifact, runtime profile, granted capabilities, authority evidence, effect budget, and trace policy
  + response contains typed result or fault, transition trace, proposed and committed effects, observations, residual uncertainty, resource use, and reentry state
  + runtime revalidates package, scope, validity, revocation, dependencies, target, entry contract, capability, authority, and budget at use time
  + effect broker distinguishes requested, authorized, denied, committed, failed, compensated, and observed
  + provider broker returns typed evidence or proposals only at the profile's declared grade

& [ExactTarget] is SOP-X
  + emits deterministic exact executable fabric and trace
  + owns no runtime grant until separately admitted
  + refuses unsupported semantic behavior instead of approximating it

& [NeuralTarget] is SOP-N
  + emits reviewed corpus contracts, routing or prompting artifacts, model blueprints, candidate initial-state constraints, training or evaluation plans, or provider packages
  + learned output is provider-dependent proposal by default
  + authoritative terms resolve back to inspectable source identities and digests rather than weights alone
  + an LLM may form candidate topology, examples, mappings, or code but cannot certify its own output
  - never: call generated tensors a correct trained model without construction, training, held-out evaluation, correspondence, and admission evidence

& [HybridTarget] is SOP-H
  + exact control requests bounded neural proposals
  + exact gates may admit, qualify, challenge, remask, branch, reject, or abstain
  + fallback remains valid when the neural path is absent, stale, uncertain, rejected, failed, or disabled
  + no neural result directly commits state or effect

& [DerivedTargetSet] is explicit
  + SOP-A projects bounded attention frames and query directives
  + SOP-D projects schemas, indexes, graph or relational views, and query plans
  + SOP-T projects typed tool and service interfaces
  + SOP-W projects workflows, dependency graphs, worker claims, and checkpoints
  + SOP-F projects interpreter-layer or native hardware artifacts under hardware-specific proof
  + SOP-I projects human or machine interfaces
  = must: use the CommonTargetABI and declare capability, proof grade, loss, nondeterminism, and provider dependence
  - never: add a target without signed requirement, measured benefit, maintenance owner, compatibility policy, and removal path

& [InstructionAndFacultyBoundary] is layered
  + DECLARE, SCOPE, RELATE, ATTEND, INFER, CONSTRAIN, TRANSFORM, CONTROL, EFFECT, and EMIT are typed instruction families
  + attention operations alter explicit frames and inference operations produce judgments under named regimes
  + Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Weaver, and Planner are compiled governed libraries over primitives, not magical keywords
  + faculty participation remains causally inspectable through activations, returns, boundaries, projections, objections, disposition, and inscription

& [EffectAndRuntimeBoundary] is fail-closed
  + pure, attention, epistemic, memory-read, memory-write, database-read, database-write, file, Git, tool, provider, user-authorization, and external effects are distinct
  + read never implies write
  + effect request binds resource, operation, authority, scope, reversibility, compensation, observation, and budget
  + compiler formation does not grant runtime capabilities
  + this purpose signature changes no external state

& [PackageLineage] is complete
  + PackageFamily binds source generations, dependencies, profiles, compiler, SemanticIR root, target artifacts, correspondence, loss, diagnostics, proofs, provider dependencies, and trust metadata
  + SJS satisfaction metadata establishes specification governance only
  + cryptographic package signatures establish content and authority admission under the Trusted Compilation Profile
  + every runtime run binds its admitted package and produces result, effect, observation, and reentry lineage

& [ConformanceAndCompatibility] is independently testable
  + equivalent verbose, condensed, and machine forms must produce one canonical SemanticIR root under the same profile
  + non-program roles remain non-executable even when instruction-shaped or signed
  + targets declare the observation boundary within which correspondence is tested
  + at least one expected-result path is independent of the compiler path under test
  + source, semantic, module, target, package, and migration compatibility are evaluated separately
  + incompatible changes create new generations and preserve original interpretation, loss, obligations, proof, rollback, and supersession

& [DiagnosticsAndFailure] preserves meaningful distinctions
  + malformed, unknown, ambiguous, contradictory, unsupported, stale, unauthorized, lossy, provider-dependent, denied, failed, partial, compensated, and unobserved are not interchangeable
  + repairs are bounded proposals and cannot silently change role, meaning, source generation, authority, or effect
  + unsupported target features or prohibited loss block lowering visibly
  + negative and no-benefit results remain valid proof artifacts

& [ReflectionAndReplay] is source-bound
  + source, profile, compiler, SemanticIR, target, package, provider, runtime, effect, observation, result, residual, and reentry identities are retained
  + inspection and debugging do not mutate the inspected authority
  + deterministic claims bind reproducible toolchain and configuration; nondeterministic claims bind known seeds and residual uncertainty

& [BootstrapAndMigration] is explicit
  + SOP may describe its own language and compiler artifacts
  + one independently trusted parser, validator, canonical serializer, signature policy, and fixture remain necessary
  + self-hosting may reduce but cannot conceal the trusted base
  + migration never overwrites preserved source or silently expands a prior signature

& [FirstImplementationFrontier] is described but not released
  + one pure typed program declares definitions, data, relation, bounded inference, constraint, unresolved alternative, denied effect, and emitted result
  + verbose, condensed, and machine surfaces converge on one SemanticIR root
  + SOP-X produces deterministic result and trace
  + SOP-N produces blueprint or provider request with proposal-only output
  + SOP-H validates or refuses a supplied neural proposal through exact gates
  + instruction-shaped data remains data and an undeclared write effect blocks
  + [implementation_authority] is absent_until_new_claimed_slice_and_profile_source

& [RequirementSet] is canonical
  + SMTC-001 through SMTC-030 are mapped in the requirement matrix
  + purpose semantics are satisfied by this canonical after valid artifact-bound phase lock
  + implementation, runtime, conformance execution, neural generation, and hardware proof remain not started

